{
  "version": 1,
  "provenance": {
    "modes": "Actual callback words establish Mode16 and TaskDesc24 records; menu allocation equals sizeof(MenuWork)=20. mode_test callbacks are physically absent in EU.",
    "font": "mode_test font encoder has two valid Shift-JIS lead-byte branches,81 and82; draw selects font bank0 or1. Four following words are independent pointers to terminated \u25cf/\u25cb/\u2605/\u2606 strings, not font entries.",
    "wrappers": "Eight pairs of native EU five-language tile and gfx arrays are referenced by55 canonical CBA8 records and106 canonical CF18 records; gfx targets are already compiler-owned native arrays and every selected index is within their actual bounds. These are graphics pointers, not LocalizedText.",
    "front_owner": "The US/JP test-mode lifecycle callbacks exclusively reference the three leading RAM words and are directly named by the native Mode record. The retained EU prefix contains its four friend-Pooh callbacks and private helper, with a native TaskDesc and name. The shared ApproachValueHalf helper retains its existing regional position. These retained prefixes precede task_lockon_0, and ordinary record definitions reproduce the separate front registration locations in each original ROM. Each regional prefix owns its descriptor name as ordinary readonly C data. The US/JP diagnostic name is exactly the ten bytes through its first terminator, with its only reference in the owning Mode record. Its original preceding zero byte is supplied by the compiler input section alignment; the unchanged following graphics retain their separate raw storage. Three private US/JP words preserve their original addresses using ordinary static definitions. This establishes the boundary before lockon, not a common semantic implementation of the regional front groups or a complete original TU for the shared math helper. The remaining mixed support code and its placements are retained separately pending further ownership evidence.",
    "mode_tail_ownership": "Deck/menu, Continue and Event callback groups each reproduce their native code, name, initialized-data and BSS runs in all three original ROMs. The shared event ID is unsigned as established by the original message-handler switch branches.",
    "font_native_owner": "The two-bank font index is read by the Shift-JIS renderer in mode_test_support.c, whose encoder selects bank 0 or 1 for lead bytes 0x81 and 0x82. Its four following pointer globals retain terminated Shift-JIS symbol strings of the same text format; no live users of those four globals are claimed. Keeping this established five-object font group with the encoder and renderer is a reconstruction assumption supported by their compatible format, unchanged regional order, and native initialized-data layout immediately after that source's Lockon descriptor. It does not assert a uniquely recovered boundary for all remaining mixed support functions. Ordinary definitions preserve all six original objects and relocations in a 48-byte section, while the separate EU-only 16-array card graphics catalog remains in mode_test_data.c as ordinary initialized data with its existing types, language order and bounds."
  },
